    <figure class="frame reveal">
      <svg class="svg-info" viewBox="0 0 400 400" role="img" aria-label="Powers of ten: from the Planck length to the observable universe">
        <g font-family="Cinzel, serif" font-size="11" fill="#f3dd9c">
          <text x="20" y="28">SCALES OF THE REAL</text>
        </g>
        <line x1="40" y1="50" x2="40" y2="370" stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="1"/>
        <g font-family="EB Garamond, serif" font-size="11" fill="#efe3c8">
          <g>
            <circle cx="40" cy="70" r="4" fill="#9b7ddb"/><text x="56" y="74">10⁻³⁵ m · Planck length</text>
            <circle cx="40" cy="108" r="4" fill="#9b7ddb"/><text x="56" y="112">10⁻¹⁵ m · proton</text>
            <circle cx="40" cy="146" r="4" fill="#6fae7f"/><text x="56" y="150">10⁻⁹ m · DNA helix width</text>
            <circle cx="40" cy="184" r="4" fill="#6fae7f"/><text x="56" y="188">10⁻⁵ m · a human cell</text>
            <circle cx="40" cy="222" r="4" fill="#d7b05a"/><text x="56" y="226">10⁰ m · you, reading</text>
            <circle cx="40" cy="260" r="4" fill="#6fae7f"/><text x="56" y="264">10⁷ m · Earth</text>
            <circle cx="40" cy="298" r="4" fill="#d7b05a"/><text x="56" y="302">10²¹ m · the Milky Way</text>
            <circle cx="40" cy="336" r="4" fill="#9b7ddb"/><text x="56" y="340">10²⁷ m · observable universe</text>
          </g>
        </g>
        <text x="56" y="366" font-family="EB Garamond, serif" font-size="10" fill="#c9bda3" font-style="italic">
          You sit almost exactly at the logarithmic midpoint.</text>
      </svg>
      <figcaption><strong>Plate II — Scales of the Real.</strong> Sixty-two orders of magnitude on one axis.
      The human body lands near the middle — not cosmically significant, but geometrically charming.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="frame reveal">
