        <text x="344" y="246" font-family="EB Garamond, serif" font-size="9" fill="#c9bda3">the loudest a sound can be in air</text>
        <text x="200" y="272" font-family="EB Garamond, serif" fill="#c9bda3" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5">Every 10 dB is ten times the intensity and about twice the perceived loudness.</text>
        <text x="200" y="288" font-family="EB Garamond, serif" fill="#c9bda3" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5">Which is why 85 dB sounds merely busy and is quietly deafening you.</text>
