      <figcaption><strong>Plate XXXV — Base Rates.</strong> The single most useful figure on this site. A very good test for a very rare thing returns mostly false alarms. Every claim of contact, every striking coincidence, every diagnosis from a single result has to be weighed against how often the thing happens at all. This is not scepticism; it is arithmetic.</figcaption>
